msgid "Installation security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:6
#: 7d5288e46186413fa7f9e3ee2b46b1bc
msgid ""
"There are several security matters to consider before and during the Qubes "
"installation process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:9
#: 236ed1ee73eb4f6ea9bff583e7a8737a
msgid "Trusting your hardware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:12
#: f97a585d4ee14347bfca1702ea34cef5
msgid ""
"No operating system, not even Qubes, can help you if you’re installing it on "
"hardware that is already compromised. This includes CPUs, GPUs, SSDs, HDDs, "
"the motherboard, BIOS/EFI/UEFI, and all relevant firmware. Unfortunately, in "
"today’s world of undetectable supply chain attacks, there are no easy "
"solutions. (Tools like :doc:`Anti Evil Maid (AEM) </user/security-in-qubes/"
"anti-evil-maid>` can help with *maintaining* the trustworthiness of your "
"hardware, but not with establishing it in the first place.) Some users have "
"chosen to use tools like `coreboot <https://www.coreboot.org/>`__, `Heads "
"<https://osresearch.net/>`__, and `Skulls <https://github.com/merge/"
"skulls>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:15
#: 3ffce5de9e0341599ae9d58e24cbb4f0
msgid "Verifying the Qubes ISO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:18
#: 40de6cdc634046d3bea9d3af61335709
msgid ""
"You should :doc:`verify </project-security/verifying-signatures>` the PGP "
"signature on your Qubes ISO before you install from it. However, if the "
"machine on which you attempt the verification process is already "
"compromised, it could falsely claim that a malicious ISO has a good "
"signature. Therefore, in order to be certain that your Qubes ISO is "
"trustworthy, you require a trustworthy machine. But how can you be certain "
"*that* machine is trustworthy? Only by using another trusted machine, and so "
"forth. This is a `classic problem <https://www.ece.cmu.edu/~ganger/712."
"fall02/papers/p761-thompson.pdf>`__. While various `solutions <https://www."
"dwheeler.com/trusting-trust/>`__ have been proposed, the point is that each "
"user must ultimately make a choice about whether to trust that a file is non-"
"malicious."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:21
#: 3fcae23af8034d9fa91a4228280b4335
msgid "Choosing an installation medium"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:24
#: f76c66a5fc6d465dad801abcccb77c48
msgid ""
"So, after taking some measures to verify its integrity and authenticity, "
"you’ve decided to trust your Qubes ISO. Great! Now you must decide what sort "
"of medium on which to write it so that you can install from it. From a Qubes-"
"specific security perspective, each has certain pros and cons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:27
#: 1698dda11a7e4dd99fda541334d4ba63
msgid "USB drives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:30
#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:50
#: cf1908f4ac0f4eb0b40c328168cbfe77 ebc6169c65144b69adaab3e5b715b8de
msgid "Pros:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:32
#: 581379eff42149ed91bac6ca89162cca
msgid ""
"Works via USB, including with a :doc:`USB qube </user/advanced-topics/usb-"
"qubes>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:34
#: 244f0649b164469d9dd4a114bd3dc4e2
msgid "Non-fixed capacity. (Easy to find one on which the ISO can fit.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:38
#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:56
#: 8821545fefd84d1689fc4a9a5b7e4a04 b46aa8570a274c049f974781b10a2e2a
msgid "Cons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:40
#: b600e563ed9e49679e92c8f3d5ac1138
msgid ""
"Rewritable. (If the drive is mounted to a compromised machine, the ISO could "
"be maliciously altered after it has been written to the drive.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:42
#: 141c39a3b1b04cc8962221ee90b05a88
msgid ""
"Untrustworthy firmware. (Firmware can be malicious even if the drive is new. "
"Plugging a drive with rewritable firmware into a compromised machine can "
"also `compromise the drive <https://web.archive.org/web/20160304013434/"
"https://srlabs.de/badusb/>`__. Installing from a compromised drive could "
"compromise even a brand new Qubes installation.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:47
#: 1d5318c9a4b04236ab1661c1f5e408c2
msgid "Optical discs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:52
#: 9067a7efcd684c6086620e4ee21137b0
msgid ""
"Read-only available. (If you use read-only media, you don’t have to worry "
"about the ISO being maliciously altered after it has been written to the "
"disc. You then have the option of verifying the signature on multiple "
"different machines.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:58
#: 8e66cd6015d1447b90fcc5107e604487
msgid ""
"Fixed capacity. (If the size of the ISO is larger than your disc, it will be "
"inconvenient.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/install-security.rst:60
#: 30a2d89deabd4c618d84f91e7dbddcea
